5 12:03:34 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Should We Believe the Economic Data or Americans’ “Lyin’” Eyes? The Answer Is Yes.]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://cosm.aei.org/should-we-believe-the-economic-data-or-americans-lyin-eyes-the-answer-is-yes">https://cosm.aei.org/should-we-believe-the-economic-data-or-americans-lyin-eyes-the-answer-is-yes</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://arnoldkling.substack.com/p/statistical-methods-links-2172025">Statistical Methods Links, 2/17/2025</a></p>]]></description><link>https://cosm.aei.org/should-we-believe-the-economic-data-or-americans-lyin-eyes-the-answer-is-yes</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://cosm.aei.org/should-we-believe-the-economic-data-or-americans-lyin-eyes-the-answer-is-yes</guid><pubDate>Mon, 17 Feb 2025 12:03:34 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Flaws in a Recent Lancet Study on Phone Use in Schools]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://www.afterbabel.com/p/lancet-study-flaws?utm_source=%2Finbox&utm_medium=reader2">https://www.afterbabel.com/p/lancet-study-flaws?utm_source=%2Finbox&utm_medium=reader2</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://arnoldkling.substack.com/p/statistical-methods-links-2172025">Statistical Methods Links, 2/17/2025</a></p>]]></description><link>https://www.afterbabel.com/p/lancet-study-flaws?utm_source=%2Finbox&amp;utm_medium=reader2</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.afterbabel.com/p/lancet-study-flaws?utm_source=%2Finbox&amp;utm_medium=reader2</guid><pubDate>Mon, 17 Feb 2025 12:03:34 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Flaws in a Recent Lancet Study on Phone Use in Schools]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>In this post, we show why the recent Lancet study’s assertions that restrictive phone policies in schools yield no benefits are unfounded. For example, the phone-policies in the ‘permissive’ vs ‘restrictive’ schools did not differ very much, their measure of academic performance was crude, and their measures of sc